---
title: Honey Oat Bites
author: graze
servings: 12
description: No-bake wholegrain oat flapjack bites with honey and mixed seeds - a homemade take on the classic honey and mixed seed flapjack.
---

Line a #20cm square tin{} with baking paper.

Melt @honey{100%g}, @golden syrup{75%g} and @butter{50%g} together in a #saucepan over low heat, stirring, until smooth and runny.

Take off the heat and stir in @light brown sugar{20%g} until dissolved.

Add @rolled oats{220%g}, @linseeds{20%g}, @sunflower seeds{20%g} and @pumpkin seeds{10%g} to the pan and mix well until everything is fully coated.

Stir in a pinch of @salt{1%pinch}.

Tip the mixture into the lined tin and press down firmly and evenly with the back of a spoon or spatula.

Chill in the fridge for at least ~chill{1%hour}, or until firm.

Turn out and cut into 12 bars or bites.

> Store in an airtight container in the fridge for up to a week.

> For a firmer, chewier bite, warm the honey mixture for a minute or two longer before adding the oats.

> For extra protein, stir in a spoonful of soy or pea protein powder with the oats.
